❓: VIP - viable, important & possible

Viable means an idea or plan is capable of working, succeeding, or surviving over time, while possible simply means something can be done.

Key Differences

• Possible: Means it can physically or logically happen, with no regard to cost, effort, or long-term survival.
• Viable: Means it can work practically, achieve its goal, and sustain itself (often financially or operationally) in the real world.
• Important: Refers to the value, priority, or impact of the goal, separate from whether it is easy or cheap to execute.

How They Connect in Projects

• Feasibility vs. Viability: A project can be possible (you have the tech to build it) and feasible (you can finish it), yet still lack viability if it costs too much money to maintain or lacks market demand.
• Minimum Viable Product (MVP): In business, a Minimum Viable Product strips a concept down to its core features to test if the idea is truly viable before spending major resources.

